WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.150
Happy Thanksgiving week.
感恩节周快乐。

2
00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:05.710
Yes, happy Thanksgiving week.
没错，感恩节周快乐。

3
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:06.690
Gobble, gobble.
咯咯，咯咯。

4
00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:10.790
And welcome to your second drink of Dunder Mifflin Infinity part two.
欢迎收看《邓德·米夫林无限》第二部分，这是你们的第二杯特饮。

5
00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:14.650
So last week we covered part one of Dunder Mifflin Infinity.
上周我们讲了《邓德·米夫林无限》的第一部分。

6
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:19.910
Now we have part two, and this is the one where Michael and Dwight drive into the lake
现在是第二部分，也就是迈克尔和德怀特开车冲进湖里的那一集，

7
00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.290
at the end of the episode.
在这一集的结尾。

8
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:21.570
Yep.
没错。

9
00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:22.830
Classic moment.
经典时刻。

10
00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:30.270
But there was a moment that would have started this episode that is just as shocking, at
但这一集原本还有一个开场，同样令人震惊，

11
00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:31.750
least for the universe of The Office.
至少在《办公室》的世界里是这样。

12
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:32.830
This was deleted.
这段被删减了。

13
00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:36.810
It did not run, but has been added back to the super fan episode.
它没有播出，但已经被加回了超级粉丝版剧集中。

14
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.730
We got a fan mail flurry about it.
我们收到了大量关于此事的粉丝来信。

15
00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:39.330
We sure did.
确实如此。

16
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.990
Stacey T and Liz E said this.
Stacey T 和 Liz E 是这样说的：

17
00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:47.710
I recently subscribed to Peacock so I could watch the super fan episodes.
我最近订阅了 Peacock，为了看超级粉丝版剧集。

18
00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:53.870
The cold open for Dunder Mifflin Infinity part two opens with Toby walking into the office
《邓德·米夫林无限》第二部分的冷开场是托比带着他的女朋友走进办公室，

19
00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:54.950
with his girlfriend.
和他的女朋友。

20
00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.730
They walk in and see Jim and Pam at reception.
他们走进来，看到吉姆和帕姆在前台。

21
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.610
Toby awkwardly kisses his girlfriend.
托比尴尬地吻了他的女朋友。

22
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:03.090
For way too long.
吻了太久了。

23
00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:07.510
And then jokes with Pam about violating his own PDA rule.
然后还跟帕姆开玩笑说他违反了自己的公共场合亲热规定。

24
00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:10.590
Did you remember this cold open exists?
你还记得有这个冷开场吗？

25
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:16.770
You talked about an alt cold open on the podcast, but this one was not mentioned.
你们在播客里提到过一个备选的冷开场，但没提这个。

26
00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.710
And Katie C wrote in about this and said,
Katie C 也写信问了这件事，她说：

27
00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.770
Ladies, you need to talk about this.
女士们，你们得聊聊这个。

28
00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.650
Angela, what have you got for us?
安吉拉，你有什么要告诉我们的吗？

29
00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.450
We definitely shot this.
我们确实拍了这一段。

30
00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:33.350
I even remember shooting it because the person who plays Toby's girlfriend is Paul's real life
我甚至记得拍摄时的情景，因为饰演托比女朋友的人是保罗现实生活中的

31
00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.370
wife, Janine.
妻子，珍妮。

32
00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:34.850
Yes!
没错！

33
00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:36.690
And we all got to hang out with her for the morning.
那天早上我们大家都和她待在一起。

34
00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:38.210
She's such a lovely person.
她是个非常可爱的人。

35
00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.870
She's really talented.
她真的很有才华。

36
00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:41.410
And I pulled a clip.
我剪辑了一段视频。

37
00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:45.290
Okay, so the very long pause you're going to hear is the kissing.
好的，你们接下来听到的那段很长的停顿就是接吻的声音。

38
00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:46.650
So, sorry about that.
抱歉啊。

39
00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:53.470
Imagine Toby sort of really lustfully kissing his girlfriend in front of Jim and Pam at reception.
想象一下托比在吉姆和帕姆面前，在接待处那种如饥似渴地吻他女朋友的样子。

40
00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:55.590
I'm a week, so.
我这周状态不行，所以。

41
00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:58.850
Hi, man.
嗨，伙计。

42
00:01:58.990 --> 00:01:59.510
Hey, guys.
嘿，各位。

43
00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.910
This is my girlfriend, Amy.
这是我女朋友，艾米。

44
00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:02.790
Hi.
嗨。

45
00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:03.350
Amy, how you doing?
艾米，你好吗？

46
00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:03.810
Nice to meet you.
很高兴见到你。

47
00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:04.210
Nice to meet you.
很高兴见到你。

48
00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.330
This is everybody else.
这是其他人。

49
00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:12.160
It's the place, so thanks for the lift.
就是这儿，谢谢你载我一程。

50
00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:12.840
Yeah, sure.
没问题。

51
00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:14.300
I'll see you tonight, right?
今晚见，好吗？

52
00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:14.760
Absolutely.
当然。

53
00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:15.680
Okay.
好的。

54
00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:24.290
Whoa.
哇。

55
00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:25.810
Easy, tiger.
别急，伙计。

56
00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:27.650
I just really like you.
我真的很喜欢你。

57
00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:28.730
Okay.
好吧。

58
00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:29.650
Bye, you guys.
再见，各位。

59
00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:30.330
Nice to meet you.
很高兴见到你。

60
00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:30.510
Bye.
再见。

61
00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:31.450
Have a great day.
祝你有愉快的一天。

62
00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.050
Whoa, Toby, watch out.
哇，托比，小心点。

63
00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.690
You're going to violate your own PDA memo.
你这是要违反你自己发的公共场合亲热备忘录了。

64
00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:40.330
I wouldn't want to do that now, would I?
我现在可不想那样做，对吧？

65
00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:42.900
Yeah.
是啊。

66
00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:43.940
How about that?
那又如何？

67
00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.020
It is such a long smooch.
这吻也太长了。

68
00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:54.260
And he's so, like, confident, which is, like, very unlike Toby.
而且他看起来好自信，这可一点都不像托比。

69
00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:54.640
Yeah.
是啊。

70
00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:55.940
And it's pretty delicious.
而且感觉相当美妙。

71
00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.240
Oh, and here's an extra piece of trivia.
哦，这里还有一个额外的小知识。

72
00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:04.560
If you watch the new series, The Paper, Janine is in the fourth episode and plays the teacher.
如果你看新剧《纸业》，珍妮在第四集里演那个老师。

73
00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:05.120
Yes.
是的。

74
00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:06.640
It's a great scene.
那场戏很棒。

75
00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:07.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

76
00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.720
We also got another letter that I thought was fun from Paige S, who said,
我们还收到了另一封我觉得很有趣的信，来自佩奇·S，她说，

77
00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:15.080
In the podcast, you mentioned changing the voice on the GPS.
在播客里，你们提到了更改GPS语音的事。

78
00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:20.380
Jenna said she didn't know you could do this, so I wanted to let you know about my favorite voices.
珍娜说她不知道可以这样做，所以我希望能告诉你们我最喜欢的语音。

79
00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.800
Growing up, my dad had it set to two different voices that he would switch between.
我小时候，我爸爸设置了两种不同的语音，他会换着来用。

80
00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:28.040
His favorites were Darth Vader and Austin Powers.
他最喜欢的是达斯·维达和奥斯汀·鲍尔斯。

81
00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.420
Darth Vader was a little harder to understand with his heavy breathing.
达斯·维达的语音因为有沉重的呼吸声，稍微有点难听清。

82
00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.580
Austin Powers was funny because when you reached your destination, he would say,
奥斯汀·鲍尔斯的很有趣，因为当你到达目的地时，他会说，

83
00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.020
Groovy driving.
开车真带劲。

84
00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:38.720
Yeah.
是啊。

85
00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:46.620
So, Jenna, when choosing your GPS voice, remember that there are more than just voices with accents.
所以，珍娜，在选择你的GPS语音时，记住不仅仅只有带口音的语音。

86
00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.720
There are also character voices.
还有角色语音。

87
00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.320
Did you know that, Angela?
你知道这个吗，安吉拉？

88
00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:51.220
I did not.
我不知道。

89
00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:52.460
I did not either.
我也不知道。

90
00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.340
Like, so what is Darth Vader's?
那，达斯·维达的语音是什么样的？

91
00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:57.060
He like, you have reached your destination.
他大概是说，你已经到达目的地了。

92
00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:58.320
I don't know.
我不知道。

93
00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.180
I mean, it's probably like, it's probably like,
我是说，可能是这样，可能是那样，

94
00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:07.460
But like, sometimes like, you need it, you need the person to talk faster.
但有时候，你需要那个人说得快一点。

95
00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:11.560
So it's like, it's not like, exit to San Clarito.
所以它不是那种，从圣克拉里塔出口出去。

96
00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:13.940
I don't know.
我不知道。

97
00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:14.320
What?
什么？

98
00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:15.660
I don't know.
我不知道。

99
00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:17.840
But now I feel like I need to search this up.
但现在我觉得我得去搜一下这个。

100
00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:23.520
If you could have anybody be the voice of your GPS, who would you want?
如果能让任何人来做你GPS的语音，你会选谁？

101
00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:25.420
I'm trying to think.
我在思考。

102
00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:28.260
I think someone with like a really velvety voice.
我在想那种声音特别丝滑的人。

103
00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.360
You know what I mean?
你懂我的意思吗？

104
00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:33.760
Like a rich timber voice.
就是那种音色醇厚的声音。

105
00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:39.260
Who was I just listening to who I just couldn't get enough of?
我刚才在听谁的歌来着，简直听不够？

106
00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:40.560
Like Barry White.
比如巴里·怀特。

107
00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:44.980
If he was telling me to exit the freeway, I'd probably just be like,
如果他让我下高速，我大概会直接说，

108
00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:46.900
Okay, Barry, I'll exit the freeway.
好的，巴里，我这就下高速。

109
00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.160
I like Jennifer Lawrence's voice.
我喜欢詹妮弗·劳伦斯的声音。

110
00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:50.080
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

111
00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:53.000
She's got like a really lovely voice to listen to.
她的声音听起来真的很悦耳。

112
00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:55.040
Maybe I'd like her to give me directions.
也许我会想让她给我指路。

113
00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:58.000
These are two very distinct choices.
这两个选择截然不同。

114
00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:02.540
Well, Angela, before we go, I thought since this is Thanksgiving week,
好吧，安吉拉，在结束之前，我想既然这周是感恩节，

115
00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.720
this would be a good time to share a little nugget from my digital clutter.
现在正是分享我数字杂物里的一点小珍藏的好时机。

116
00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:14.180
It is the storyline for a lost Thanksgiving episode of The Office.
这是《办公室》一集遗失的感恩节剧集的剧情大纲。

117
00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:17.000
I have been so tickled about this.
我一直为此感到特别兴奋。

118
00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:19.400
You mentioned it to me and I'm like, what?
你跟我提过这事，我当时就想，什么？

119
00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:23.480
Because we always say there wasn't a true Thanksgiving episode of The Office.
因为我们总说《办公室》没有真正意义上的感恩节特辑。

120
00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:27.720
Yeah, I have been holding on to this for so long.
是啊，我把这个藏了太久了。

121
00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:30.480
I found an old file with a bunch of story pitches.
我翻到了一个旧文件夹，里面有很多剧情构思。

122
00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:35.260
And there was one in the season three file called Thanksgiving.
在第三季的文件夹里有一个叫“感恩节”的构思。

123
00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.220
It's pretty wild.
这真的很疯狂。

124
00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:40.480
Now, just remember, this is just a pitch document.
记住，这只是一个构思文档。

125
00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:45.300
It was never written, but it gives you a glimpse at what our writers would put together.
它从未被写成剧本，但能让你一窥我们的编剧当时想写些什么。

126
00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.340
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

127
00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:47.300
Are you going to read it to us?
你要读给我们听吗？

128
00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:47.620
Yes.
是的。

129
00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:47.880
Okay.
好的。

130
00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:48.680
Here it is.
就在这儿。

131
00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.260
It is Wednesday of Thanksgiving week.
那是感恩节那一周的周三。

132
00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:55.940
We start in the kitchen where Angela enters and no one will talk to her.
故事从厨房开始，安吉拉走了进来，但没人理她。

133
00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:03.760
In a talking head, Phyllis mentions that Angela is suing the company for $8.6 million because of Oscar's slap.
在采访镜头里，菲利斯提到安吉拉因为奥斯卡的掌掴正在起诉公司，索赔860万美元。

134
00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:15.540
So, I guess during season three, before this episode, there was a pitch that for some reason I could not figure out why Oscar was going to have slapped Angela.
所以，我想在第三季这一集之前，曾有过一个构思，但我实在想不出为什么奥斯卡会扇安吉拉耳光。

135
00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:18.740
She was probably being a real bitch and he had had it.
她当时可能真的很刻薄，而他忍无可忍了。

136
00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:19.200
All right.
好吧。

137
00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:22.820
So, now we find out that Michael has chosen to ignore this lawsuit.
现在我们发现迈克尔选择无视这场诉讼。

138
00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:25.760
It doesn't name him personally, so it's not his problem.
因为诉讼没点他的名，所以不是他的问题。

139
00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:29.940
He is also excited because he's going to spend Thanksgiving with Carol.
他也很兴奋，因为他要和卡罗尔一起过感恩节。

140
00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:34.880
Dwight is nervous because the shrewd Thanksgiving is going to be at Shrewd Farms this year.
德怀特很紧张，因为今年的施鲁特感恩节要在施鲁特农场举行。

141
00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:39.720
And moreover, he has decided to have his girlfriend meet his family.
而且，他决定带女朋友去见家人。

142
00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:45.920
His girlfriend being Angela, although he doesn't tell everyone in the office who he means.
他的女朋友就是安吉拉，尽管他没告诉办公室里的其他人他指的是谁。

143
00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.380
Well, Michael hears about the shrewd gathering and the document says he shits on it.
迈克尔听说了施鲁特的聚会，文档里说他对此嗤之以鼻。

144
00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:54.740
Michael says, a hundred shrewds in one barn?
迈克尔说，一百个施鲁特挤在一个谷仓里？

145
00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:55.940
Dork convention.
书呆子大会吗。

146
00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:59.280
So, now Carol comes to see Michael at the office.
这时，卡罗尔来办公室找迈克尔。

147
00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:04.000
She says, this is hard, but I think my kids should be with their father on Thanksgiving.
她说，这很难开口，但我认为我的孩子们感恩节应该和他们的父亲在一起。

148
00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:05.680
So, we're driving to Maryland.
所以，我们要开车去马里兰州。

149
00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:09.000
Michael says, that's going to be awkward.
迈克尔说，那会很尴尬吧。

150
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.260
Is Rick going to be okay with me being there?
瑞克会介意我在场吗？

151
00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:12.900
Carol says, no.
卡萝尔说不行。

152
00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:14.900
That's why you're not coming.
这就是你不能去的原因。

153
00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:21.900
Then, in a talking head, Carol reveals that she's been reconciling with her ex and is essentially calling it off by going there.
随后，在一段访谈中，卡萝尔透露她一直在和前任复合，这次去其实就是为了彻底了断。

154
00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:26.960
Though, Michael doesn't necessarily realize the long-term implications of her actions.
不过，迈克尔并没有意识到她这么做会有什么长远的影响。

155
00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:31.140
So, now, Michael is sad because he has no place to go.
所以现在，迈克尔很伤心，因为他没地方可去了。

156
