还有，朱莉，我们没拍那种你在电影里可能看到的深吻之类的镜头。

328
00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:37.580
This was like television comedy.
这是电视喜剧。

329
00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:41.880
Kissing is very different than like a dramatic movie.
接吻和剧情片里的吻戏非常不同。

330
00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:46.100
Make out, you know, it's your lips are kind of just together.
那种亲热戏，你知道，就是嘴唇贴在一起而已。

331
00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:47.460
You know, you kind of fake it.
你知道，就是假装一下。

332
00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:49.220
Fakey kiss, fakey bag.
假装亲吻，假装亲热。

333
00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:53.860
Well, our next question comes from Jessica Willis.
好的，下一个问题来自杰西卡·威利斯。

334
00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:59.820
I've always been curious, how much ADR did you have to typically do for your episodes?
我一直很好奇，你们通常需要为剧集补录多少后期配音？

335
00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:05.940
I've noticed that in some episodes, you see characters remove a mic pack and the audio goes
我注意到在某些剧集中，你会看到角色摘下麦克风，然后音频就

336
00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:06.260
black.
没了。

337
00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:10.180
It's such a real cool detail and a reference to the documentary.
这是一个非常酷的细节，也是对纪录片形式的致敬。

338
00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:17.180
So how much original audio did you use and how much was re-recorded after filming?
那么你们用了多少原始音频，又有多少是在拍摄后重新录制的？

339
00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:21.620
Well, lady, my memory is we did not do a lot of ADr.
嗯，这位女士，我的记忆里是我们没做过多少后期配音。

340
00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:26.020
I mean, I have one memory of the whole nine years of going in to do it.
我是说，在整整九年里，我只记得有一次去录音棚补录。

341
00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:26.620
Yeah.
是的。

342
00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:31.360
In the entire nine years, I only recorded one line that they had to dub in later.
在整整九年里，我只录过一句后来需要配音的台词。

343
00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:32.640
One in nine years.
九年里就一句。

344
00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:34.560
And I thought that's how it worked.
我还以为工作都是这样的呢。

345
00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:35.340
Yeah.
是啊。

346
00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:42.940
And when I went on other jobs, part of your job is you go in a studio every week and you
后来我去做其他工作时，工作的一部分就是每周都要去录音棚，

347
00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:48.680
dub lines that got missed or that maybe a plane flew over your head or there was a sound
补录那些漏掉的台词，或者可能因为头顶飞过飞机，或者有声音

348
00:17:48.680 --> 00:17:51.220
problem and they dump it in.
问题而需要补录的台词。

349
00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:56.020
And I'd spend maybe 30 minutes an hour just doing that on other shows.
在其他剧组，我可能得花半小时到一个小时做这些事。

350
00:17:56.180 --> 00:17:57.480
But on our show, we did not.
但在我们的剧组，我们不需要。

351
00:17:57.600 --> 00:17:58.560
And why is that, Jenna?
那是为什么呢，珍娜？

352
00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:03.780
Because same, all the other projects I've gone on, you have like an ADR day where you
因为同样地，我参与过的所有其他项目，你都会有一个ADR（后期对白录音）日，你需要

353
00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:04.380
go in.
去录音棚。

354
00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:08.180
But on The Office, I only did ADR once and it was for the finale.
但在《办公室》里，我只做过一次ADR，那是为了大结局。

355
00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:14.060
And I got to see footage of the finale before it aired, before anyone saw it because I went
我得以在大结局播出前，在任何人看到之前就看到了片段，因为我去了

356
00:18:14.060 --> 00:18:15.760
in and had to loop one line.
录音棚，必须补录一句台词。

357
00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:20.940
And it was because we were outside and we had that storm coming in and they just needed
那是因为我们在户外拍摄，当时有暴风雨要来，他们只是需要

358
00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:22.080
me to loop a line.
我补录一句台词。

359
00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:26.320
And I even took a picture in the ADR booth because I'd never been in there.
我甚至在ADR录音间里拍了张照片，因为我以前从没进去过。

360
00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:33.100
You know, first of all, our sound engineers were Emmy award winning.
你知道，首先，我们的音效工程师是艾美奖得主。

361
00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:35.740
They won Emmys for their sound design on our show.
他们凭借我们剧集的音效设计赢得了艾美奖。

362
00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:36.820
They're just amazing.
他们简直太棒了。

363
00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:40.840
But they also had a mic pack on every single actor.
而且他们还在每一位演员身上都装了麦克风包。

364
00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:45.940
We had two boom operators in the room and they hid microphones throughout the office.
我们在房间里有两名吊杆话筒操作员，他们还在办公室各处隐藏了麦克风。

365
00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:47.080
I had one at reception.
我在接待处就有一个。

366
00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:47.780
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

367
00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:53.620
Yeah, we had a microphone in the accounting pod and they put it next to Oscar's phone.
是的，我们在会计部有一个麦克风，他们把它放在了奥斯卡的电话旁边。

368
00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:57.320
So it would sort of pick up the three of us, you know?
这样它就能收录到我们三个人的声音，你懂的？

369
00:18:57.880 --> 00:19:04.560
But I also remember I would often see our boom operators and camera operators having little
但我还记得，我经常看到我们的吊杆操作员和摄像师进行小型的

370
00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:10.860
powwows because they would have to choreograph the boom swing with the camera swing so that
碰头会，因为他们必须协调吊杆的摆动和摄像机的移动，这样

371
00:19:10.860 --> 00:19:12.940
they could pick up the sound.
他们才能收录到声音。

372
00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:17.620
And it was this crafted dance that they did.
那是一场他们精心编排的舞蹈。

373
00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:19.400
And it's really amazing.
真的非常了不起。

374
00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:23.660
And I'm actually glad that Jessica wrote in because it gives us a chance to really shout
我其实很高兴杰西卡写信来，因为这让我们有机会好好地

375
00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:25.660
out our sound department, which was incredible.
感谢我们的音效部门，他们真是太棒了。

376
00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:30.280
Our main guys that were with us on the stage were Ben Patrick.
我们在片场的主要负责人是本·帕特里克。

377
00:19:31.340 --> 00:19:31.860
Yep.
没错。

378
00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:36.500
He was our main like production sound mixer, sound editor.
他是我们主要的制作混音师和音效剪辑师。

379
00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:39.700
And we had our two boom operators, Nick Carbone.
我们还有两位吊杆操作员，尼克·卡博内。

380
00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:40.980
Don't get Carboned.
别被“卡博内”了。

381
00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:42.840
Don't get Carboned.
别被“卡博内”了。

382
00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:44.300
And Brian Whittle.
还有布莱恩·惠特尔。

383
00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:51.880
Brian Whittle would be the inspiration for the boom operator that we see later in the
布莱恩·惠特尔就是后来我们在剧中看到的那个吊杆操作员的灵感来源。

384
00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:52.240
season.
在故事里，是的。

385
00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:52.980
In the story, yeah.
但在那之外，我们还有混音部门，还有其他的吊杆操作员和轮换人员。

386
00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:58.400
But then we also had like a mixing department and we had other boom operators and people that
我们真的有一个非常出色的音效团队。

387
00:19:58.400 --> 00:19:59.120
would rotate in.
是的，他们太棒了。

388
00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:01.100
We just had a really amazing sound team.
好吧，我们还有一个问题。

389
00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:02.260
Yeah, they were great.
这个问题来自艾丽西亚·W。

390
00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:04.100
Well, we have one more question.
她问，在那些摄像机对着办公室拍摄的访谈片段中，斯坦利

