莱斯利·大卫·贝克在拍摄访谈片段时，必须一直待在背景里吗？

393
00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:13.500
almost always in the background.
还是说那个背景是后期合成进去的？

394
00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:19.260
Would Leslie David Baker have to stay in the background the whole time they filmed talking
哦，艾丽西亚。

395
00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:19.740
heads?
他必须坐在那里。

396
00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:22.040
Or was that background edited in?
是的。

397
00:20:22.180 --> 00:20:23.020
Oh, Alicia.
整整九年。

398
00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:24.520
He had to sit there.
他必须坐在那里。

399
00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:25.160
Yes.
是的。

400
00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:26.560
For nine years.
整整九年。

401
00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:28.920
Poor Leslie David Baker.
可怜的莱斯利·大卫·贝克。

402
00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:31.120
He was always in the background.
他总是待在背景里。

403
00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:32.700
He was always there.
他一直都在那儿。

404
00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:34.840
You could see him at his desk.
你能看到他坐在办公桌前。

405
00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:37.820
And he was such a trooper.
他真是个尽职尽责的好演员。

406
00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:42.160
When people had talking heads, when we had a long day of them, he'd sit there.
当人们进行访谈拍摄时，如果拍摄时间很长，他就会一直坐在那儿。

407
00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:42.560
Yep.
没错。

408
00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:46.780
And sometimes Phyllis would have to sit there and sometimes Creed as well.
有时候菲利斯也得坐在那儿，有时克里德也是。

409
00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:47.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

410
00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:48.120
Yes.
是的。

411
00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:54.200
And early on, they would have people there designated to cross.
在早期，他们会指定一些人走动。

412
00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:58.220
Like you might see someone like cross to the kitchen or cross back.
比如你可能会看到有人走去厨房或者走回来。

413
00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:01.880
We abandoned that after a couple of seasons.
几季之后我们就放弃这种做法了。

414
00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:06.420
I think if you look at early season talking heads, you see crosses in the background.
我想如果你看早期剧集的访谈片段，就能看到背景里有人走动。

415
00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:11.300
And then at a certain point, people were like, I think I'm thinking, no, I think I'm not going
后来到了某个阶段，大家就觉得，我在想，不，我觉得我不想

416
00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:14.720
to go to the kitchen and back to get a cup of coffee for two hours.
为了倒杯咖啡，在两小时内走去厨房再走回来。

417
00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:15.420
Yeah.
是啊。

418
00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:20.420
I don't, also, I think they were a little distracting because I know I did a cross one time and they
而且，我觉得这有点让人分心，因为我知道有一次我走动的时候，他们

419
00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:23.960
had me cross really close to the conference room, that cabinet that was there.
让我从会议室旁边那个柜子附近走过去。

420
00:21:24.020 --> 00:21:25.020
And then they're like, eh, no.
然后他们就说，呃，算了。

421
00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:27.040
And then they had me cross way in the back.
接着他们让我从很远的地方走过去。

422
00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:30.140
But I think ultimately they were just like, okay, no, no crossing.
但我觉得最终他们决定，好吧，不准走动了。

423
00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:34.440
Well, also, if you wanted to improv, it would throw off the timing of the cross.
而且，如果你想即兴发挥，走动的时机就会被打乱。

424
00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:34.740
Yeah.
没错。

425
00:21:34.900 --> 00:21:38.360
And so you would, when you went into editing, it did not work for crosses.
所以当你进入剪辑阶段时，走动镜头根本用不上。

426
00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:41.580
It just worked to have poor Leslie at his desk.
还是让可怜的莱斯利坐在桌前最合适。

427
00:21:41.680 --> 00:21:41.880
Yes.
是的。

428
00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:42.640
As a constant.
作为一个固定的背景。

429
00:21:43.460 --> 00:21:44.660
Leslie and then Creed.
莱斯利，然后是克里德。

430
00:21:44.660 --> 00:21:44.710
Creed.
克里德。

431
00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:47.080
I think Creed would be the number two runner up for that.
我觉得克里德应该是排在第二位的。

432
00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:48.540
I think so too.
我也这么认为。

433
00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:53.900
And then before we go to break, we just got a really nice comment and it made us happy.
在进入休息时间之前，我们刚收到一条非常好的评论，让我们很开心。

434
00:21:53.900 --> 00:21:54.920
So we thought we'd share it.
所以我们想分享一下。

435
00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:56.520
It is from Cecilia B.
来自塞西莉亚·B。

436
00:21:56.800 --> 00:22:01.300
And she says, ladies, I have to tell you, you two are amazing.
她说，女士们，我必须告诉你们，你们俩太棒了。

437
00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:02.860
Thank you, Cecilia.
谢谢你，塞西莉亚。

438
00:22:02.860 --> 00:22:07.260
I finally got the courage to ask for our changes at work.
我终于鼓起勇气在工作中提出了我们的诉求。

439
00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:12.440
And all I kept hearing was both of you ladies in my head saying, just go for it.
我脑子里一直回响着你们两位女士的话，说，去争取吧。

440
00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:14.200
Ask for what you want.
去争取你想要的。

441
00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:17.160
And I'm so happy that I listened to you ladies.
我很高兴我听了你们的话。

